  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_6+\\mathrm{HNO}_3 \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{NO}_2+\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}$ $78 \\mathrm{~g} \\quad 123 \\mathrm{~g}$ Now since $78 \\mathrm{~g}$ of benzene on nitration give $=123 \\mathrm{~g}$ nitrobenzene hence $5 \\mathrm{~g}$ of benzene on nitration give $=\\frac{123}{78} \\times 5=7.88 \\mathrm{~g}$\nnearest answer is (c) i.e. theoritical yield $=7.88 \\mathrm{~g}$",
